---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Data Safety – KAOS" description="KAOS data safety summary: what the game collects, why, and how to delete it.">
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Data safety</p>
      <h1>Data safety.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A plain summary of the data KAOS handles, matching the Data safety section on Google Play.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <article class="container prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated: October 2026.</strong></p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>KAOS has no ads and no analytics, and it does not run its own servers. It only handles leaderboard data when you choose to sign in to the optional leaderboards through Google Play Games Services. The game is fully playable offline.</p>

      <h2>Data collected</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Data type</th><th>What exactly</th><th>Collected</th><th>Shared</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th>Personal info → User IDs</th>
            <td>Your Google Play Games player ID, provided by Play Games when you sign in</td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-yes">Yes, optional</span></td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-no">No</span></td>
            <td>App functionality (leaderboards)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>App activity → Other in-game actions</th>
            <td>Survival time / score</td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-yes">Yes, optional</span></td>
            <td><span class="pill pill-no">No</span></td>
            <td>App functionality (rankings)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>“Optional” means nothing leaves your device for the leaderboards unless you sign in through Play Games and submit a score. Play Games is a Google service that processes this data on our behalf under Google's terms and privacy policy. Your Play Games player name and score are visible to other players.</p>

      <h2>Data we do not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No email address, password, phone number, or contact list.</li>
        <li>No precise or approximate location.</li>
        <li>No photos, videos, audio, files, or messages.</li>
        <li>No health, financial, or payment information.</li>
        <li>No web browsing history or app usage analytics.</li>
        <li>No device advertising ID and no cross-app tracking.</li>
        <li>Motion/accelerometer readings are processed on-device and never sent.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>We do not sell or share your data. Leaderboard data is processed by Google Play Games Services on our behalf, under Google's terms and privacy policy. If you use the Android share sheet, the text goes only to the app you pick.</p>

      <h2>Security practices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Encrypted in transit:</strong> Play Games Services communicates over HTTPS.</li>
        <li><strong>No account data at rest on our side:</strong> we do not hold emails, passwords, or payment data.</li>
        <li><strong>Deletion request:</strong> you can delete your Play Games data through your Google account, or ask us for help.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Ads and analytics</h2>
      <p>KAOS has no advertising, no analytics, and no third-party tracking SDKs. The third-party components are the Godot game engine and Google Play Games Services.</p>

      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>Local scores and settings are deleted when you clear KAOS's app data or uninstall the game. Leaderboard data can be managed or deleted through your Google account; if you need help, email <a href="mailto:emavgl.app@gmail.com">emavgl.app@gmail.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>KAOS is a general-audience game and is not designed for children under 13. Leaderboards are optional and require a Google Play Games account, which is subject to Google's age requirements.</p>

      <p class="small-note">See the full <a href={`${base}privacy-policy`}>Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href={`${base}terms-of-service`}>Terms of Service</a> for details and your rights.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
